<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Dalian</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Dairen, Dalny</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Dalian is a port city in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/liaoning">Liaoning</a> province, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a>, near the southern tip of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/liaodong">Liaodong</a> peninsula. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a> founded it in 1898 as the commercial port of Dalny within its Kwantung lease, and after 1905 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/japan">Japan</a> developed it as Dairen, headquarters of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/south-manchuria-railway">South Manchuria Railway Company</a> and one of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/east-asia">East Asia</a>'s busiest harbours. It returned to China after 1945 and now includes <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lushunkou">Lüshunkou</a>, the former Port Arthur.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/dalian.jpg" alt="Dalian" width="320" height="212" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Fumihiko Ueno · CC BY 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Xigang,_Dalian,_Liaoning,_China_-_panoramio_(18).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
